# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both Dockerfiles install their own dependencies inside the image — Dockerfile.python
# runs `uv sync`, Dockerfile.node runs `pnpm install`. Shipping the host's trees is
# therefore pure cost, and for .venv it is also wrong: Dockerfile.python does
# `COPY . /app` and then puts /app/.venv/bin on PATH, so a macOS virtualenv would
# land darwin binaries in a linux image.
#
# Without this file the context is ~2.3GB (987MB node_modules + 1.2GB .venv), sent
# once per service build.

# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.venv

# Version control and local tooling state.
.git
.github
.husky

# Python caches and build artefacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# JS/TS build outputs — regenerated by the image build.
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage

# Local environment. .env.example is intentionally kept: compose reads it as env_file.
.env
.env.local

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/*.log
